## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a production-grade control plane feature that enforces resource fairness, minimizes disruption, and scales across tenants and clusters.

## Key Concepts
- CRD-driven budgets per node and per-namespace priorities
- Reconciliation loop with breach detection, drain/re-schedule, and preemption safety
- Interaction with PodDisruptionBudget, CSI volumes, and QoS tiers
- Observability: metrics, alerts, audit trails, and tracing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo reconciler skeleton for NodeBudget controller
class NodeBudgetController {
  reconcile(nodeBudgetCR) {
    const node = getNode(nodeBudgetCR.spec.nodeName)
    const budget = nodeBudgetCR.spec.budget
    const usage = getNodeUsage(node)
    if (usage.cpu > budget.cpu || usage.mem > budget.mem) {
      const candidates = selectNonCriticalPods(node)
      drainPods(candidates)
      rescheduleToHealthyNodes(candidates)
      emitEventsAndMetrics(node, usage, budget)
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model priority and fairness when multiple nodes breach budgets simultaneously?
- How would you test this with a simulated workload and ensure no data loss during drains?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a Kubernetes-native multi-tenant shard architecture, implement operator-driven lifecycle management, and construct safe upgrade and backup workflows—essential skills for building scalable platforms serving multiple customers.

## Key Concepts

- CustomResourceDefinition design and operator reconciliation loops
- StatefulSets with per-tenant PVCs and resource quotas
- Canary rollouts with per-tenant rate limiting
- Cross-tenant backup orchestration and disaster recovery
- PodDisruptionBudgets for controlling upgrade blast radius

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo reconciliation loop
async function reconcileTenantShard(cr) {
  const ns = cr.metadata.namespace;
  await ensureNamespace(ns);
  const sts = buildStatefulSet(cr);
  await applyStatefulSet(sts);
  const pdb = buildPodDisruptionBudget(cr);
  await applyPDB(pdb);
  const backupJob = buildBackupJob(cr);
  await scheduleBackup(backupJob);
  await updateStatus(cr, { phase: 'Ready' });
}
```
